\label{thm1}
There is a Feller process $((X_t)_{t>0},(P^x)_{x\in F})$ on the Sierpi\'nski carpet $F$ with a transition density $q_t(x,y)$ satisfying the two-sided sub-Gaussian heat kernel estimate 
\begin{equation}\label{e:1.1}
	\begin{split} 
		C_1\frac{1}{\mu(B(x,t^{1/\beta}))}\exp(-C_2(\frac{|x-y|^{\beta}}{t})^{\frac{1}{\beta-1}})&\leq q_t(x,y)\\&\leq C_3\frac{1}{\mu(B(x,t^{1/\beta}))}\exp(-C_4(\frac{|x-y|^{\beta}}{t})^{\frac{1}{\beta-1}})
	\end{split} 
\end{equation}
for all $x,y\in F$ and $t\leq 1$.

