Let $d\in\mathbb{N}$ such that $d\geq 2$. 
Assume the data ${\bf a}$, $a_0,S,g$ are smooth enough and the characteristic curves fullfill the domain $\mathbb{R}^d_+$. Then, for all compact sets $X \subset \mathbb{R}^d_+$, there exist constants $C_X^{(0)}, \dots, C_X^{(3)} >0$ which do not depend on $h$, $\varepsilon$, $\Delta s$, such that, if $C_X^{(0)}\,\Delta s  \leq h,$
the approximation $\tilde u^{\varepsilon,\Delta s}_h$ given by the scheme
\begin{equation}
